ups-pi-node (0.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add the root-owned Go helper with direct NetworkManager D-Bus access.
  * Make managed Wi-Fi profiles idempotent and stabilize hotspot fallback.
  * Move INA3221, GPIO relay control, and the ST7735 renderer to Go.
  * Add a Go HTTP/SSE service and responsive animated power dashboard.
  * Package both runtimes with transactional health-checked rollback.

 -- Pavlo <pavlo@example.com>  Sun, 19 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0300

ups-pi-node (0.2.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Replace the INA219 current monitor backend with INA3221 channel support.
  * Configure the FL-2C 20 A / 75 mV external shunt at 0.00375 ohm.
  * Preserve bidirectional current readings and add configurable polarity.
  * Add INA3221 register conversion tests and migration defaults.
  * Monitor the 19 V output voltage, current, and power on INA3221 channel 2.
  * Show channel 2 output telemetry in the web UI, TFT, and integrations.
  * Clarify TFT telemetry with separate BAT and OUT voltage/current labels.
  * Add a two-card TFT dashboard rendered with Ubuntu and Ubuntu Mono fonts.
  * Add a stacked 128x160 portrait layout selected from the display bounds.

 -- Pavlo <pavlo@example.com>  Thu, 16 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0300

ups-pi-node (0.2.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Switch local package builds from timestamp versions to Debian revisions.
  * Add manual Wi-Fi scan action to the portal.
  * Restore ST7735 backlight control on GPIO18 and initialize it after the
    display driver.
  * Prevent system helper stop from deadlocking inside socketserver shutdown.
  * Migrate existing node configs with the ST7735 display defaults.
  * Hold the ST7735 backlight high using the same setup/output order as the
    verified hardware test.

 -- Pavlo <pavlo@example.com>  Thu, 14 May 2026 14:20:00 +0300

ups-pi-node (0.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Restore hardware UPS control through the system helper service.
  * Add ST7735 display support, helper-side PAM login, and hotspot password
    settings.
  * Enable Raspberry Pi I2C/SPI hardware buses during package setup.
  * Package the app for Debian Trixie with venv-based Python dependencies.

